1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,040
Medication-related dizziness — if it started after a new prescription, save this before you forget.

2
00:00:07,360 --> 00:00:10,560
The pills you're taking could be part of the problem.

3
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:19,200
Falls are the leading cause of injury-related death among older adults in the US, according to the CDC.

4
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:29,680
Certain drug classes are especially likely to trigger dizziness: blood pressure medications, benzodiazepines and sleep aids, and antihistamines.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:37,760
Taking five or more medications at once — a pattern doctors call polypharmacy — raises the risk even further.

6
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:40,560
First, blood pressure medications.

7
00:00:40,880 --> 00:00:49,760
They can cause orthostatic hypotension, a sudden drop in blood pressure when you stand up, leaving you lightheaded or briefly faint.

8
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:58,800
Sit on the edge of the bed or chair for a few seconds before standing, especially first thing in the morning or after using the bathroom.

9
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:02,960
Rising slowly gives your blood pressure time to catch up.

10
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:06,720
Second, benzodiazepines and sleep aids.

11
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:15,600
These can linger in your system well into the next day, slowing your reactions and leaving you drowsy or unsteady on your feet.

12
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:20,560
Move carefully and turn on the lights during nighttime bathroom trips.

13
00:01:20,880 --> 00:01:29,440
If grogginess lasts into the morning, ask your doctor whether an earlier dose or a shorter-acting option makes sense for you.

14
00:01:29,760 --> 00:01:31,920
Third, antihistamines.

15
00:01:32,240 --> 00:01:40,720
Older, first-generation antihistamines cross into the brain and can cause both drowsiness and dizziness as a side effect.

16
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:47,040
Ask your pharmacist about switching to a non-drowsy, second-generation antihistamine.

17
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:55,360
If you've already taken a first-generation one, hold off on driving or climbing stairs until the effect wears off.

18
00:01:55,680 --> 00:02:08,960
Rising slowly for blood pressure medications, adjusting timing for sleep aids, and switching to non-drowsy antihistamines — these three habits noticeably cut medication-related dizziness.

19
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:16,480
If you're taking five or more medications, ask your doctor or pharmacist for a full medication review.

20
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:25,280
And if dizziness starts after a new prescription, don't just stop taking it — talk to the provider who prescribed it first.
